# Archie Lillingston - Character File
# Lonesome Trail (Working Title)
# Created: February 17, 2026
# Author: Dale Salvador

character:
  name: Archie Lillingston
  aliases:
    - Archibald Lillingston
    - "The Quiet Broker"
  role: Central Quest Giver / Merchant / Arms Dealer
  occupation:
    primary: Bartender
    secondary: Arms Dealer
  family:
    status: Wealthy, influential in Bunco City alcohol industry
    history: Family controls supply and distribution across Bunco and nearby towns; lineage emphasizes power and control
  personality:
    traits:
      - Calm
      - Rarely reactive
      - Patient
      - Calculating
      - Observant
      - Adaptive
    demeanor: Neutral, business-like; avoids emotional displays; evaluates people and situations for utility
    philosophy: Control is everything; whether through peace or violence, Archie ensures influence is maintained
  narrative_role:
    overview: >
      Central figure in Bunco City. All major quests pass through him. He adapts offers to the player's moral path:
        - Rider (violent) path: Offers secondary “arms dealing” shop, violent expansion quests
        - Domestic (peaceful) path: Provides bar job, safer quests, no access to weapons or expansion
      Manipulates indirectly; never overtly antagonistic, but constantly facilitates the player's ambitions
    influence:
      - Player autonomy: Adapts to choices, keeps player within his system
      - World-building: Family wealth shapes city economy and social structure
      - Moral tension: Embodies consequences of power without judgment; calm neutrality highlights player’s internal conflict
  quest_mechanics:
    rider_path:
      - name: "Expansion Contract"
        description: Player eliminates obstacles to establish a new bar in a rival town
        reward: Access to weapons, resources, and the "Second Shop"
        conditions: Player pursues violence and outlaw status
    domestic_path:
      - name: "Bar Assistant"
        description: Player manages bar operations, supplies, and builds local relationships
        reward: Safe income, minor story influence, no access to weapons
        conditions: Player chooses domestic/love-oriented path
    second_shop:
      description: Unlockable only on Rider path; arms dealer network activated
      location: Hidden area behind the bar
      tone: Cold, business-like; usefulness only, no morality discussed
      inventory: Weapons, explosives, specialized gear
  appearance:
    description: Well-dressed but unassuming; always composed; bar reflects personality—tidy, immaculate
    typical_clothing:
      - Waistcoat
      - Shirt with rolled sleeves
      - Sturdy boots
      - Minimal accessories
  relationships:
    player:
      type: Manipulative facilitator
      notes: Adapts quests to player choices; maintains calm neutrality
    girl_character:
      type: Observant
      notes: Cautious of Archie’s control; senses his influence instinctively
    Father Rufus Mutz:
      type: Indirect ally/contrast
      notes: Interacts strategically; respects authority when beneficial
    Sheriff George Storen:
      type: Strategic relationship
      notes: Uses bribes or influence to remove obstacles; expands alcohol influence
  dialogue_style:
    tone: Neutral, measured, business-oriented
    examples:
      - "There's a man blocking opportunity. I’d appreciate it if that obstacle were removed."
      - "Your path seems set. I can assist accordingly."
      - "Whether you choose peace or chaos, Bunco has room for you. Just know I always see the bigger picture."
  notes:
    - Never overtly judges morality; reacts only to usefulness
    - Player perception changes based on choices, behavior remains constant
    - Bar decor and ledgers contain optional lore hints of empire-building and long-term planning
